## Dataset

**File:** `circuits.csv`, 77 rows and 9 columns, with no blank or `\N` values.

**Source:** Formula 1 circuits data, based on the circuits table of the Formula 1 World Championship dataset on Kaggle. https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rohanrao/formula-1-world-championship-1950-2020

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `circuit_id` | integer (primary key) | Unique ID for each circuit |
| `circuit_ref` | varchar(90) | Short lowercase reference, such as `red_bull_ring` |
| `name` | varchar(90) | Full circuit name |
| `location` | varchar(90) | City or area |
| `country` | varchar(90) | Country name |
| `latitude` | double precision | Latitude in decimal degrees |
| `longitude` | double precision | Longitude in decimal degrees |
| `altitude` | integer | Altitude in meters above sea level |
| `url` | text | Wikipedia page for the circuit |

