## Data Quality Notes

Checking the data before analyzing it turned up several things worth knowing:

| Issue | Detail | How it is handled |
|---|---|---|
| **Inconsistent country label** | The USA appears as `USA` (11 circuits) and `United States` (1 circuit) | Cleaned with a `CASE` expression in the queries where it matters (Q2, Q7). The raw table is not modified. |
| **No missing values** | No blank or `\N` values in any column | No NULL handling needed, though queries still use safe habits such as `NULLS LAST` where relevant |
| **Percent-encoded URLs** | 7 URLs contain encoded accents, like `N%C3%BCrburgring` | Documented as a limitation in Q9. PostgreSQL has no built-in URL decoder. |
| **URL anchors** | 2 URLs end with a section anchor, such as `#Circuit` | Stripped with `SPLIT_PART(url, '#', 1)` before extracting the page name |
| **Mixed URL schemes** | URLs use both `http://` and `https://` | Not an issue, because the extraction works on the text after the last `/` |
| **Near-duplicate venues** | Two Las Vegas entries sit about 190 m apart | Kept as separate rows and discussed in Q10 |

